WEBVTT

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:06.770
Time has gone by fast since we punched through the Big Barrier.

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.800
The substitute pilot is like this.

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.040
The Captain is like this.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.530
And we still made it to Mars. Isn't that amazing?

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:19.070
But are we really going to be able to win?

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:56.980
Sort of Like a "Fateful Decision"

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.070
Want a piece of me?

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.110
Let's go!

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:11.560
Hikaru!

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:14.940
Right! Right!

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:19.350
There! A nice flower garden!

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.820
Keep playing around, and you're destined for a casket.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.860
What brought that up all of a sudden?!

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:29.490
You're so fixated on being a hard-boiled show-off.

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.550
Beyond this thin hull, there lies a hellish vacuum.

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.910
As I lay waste to machine insects with no hearts,

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:41.100
my heart, amidst all of this excitement, remains

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.120
unstirred.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:46.720
I'm sorry. That's just how I am.

00:02:46.990 --> 00:02:48.720
Jeez, what a weirdo.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.140
Weirdo, weirdo!

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.090
What the hell's going on?

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:57.980
Aren't they having a lot of fun!

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:08.320
I hate inertia! Damn it!

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.460
Captain!

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.430
Recall the Aestivalis!

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:28.980
There's no need to.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:29.880
Akito, fight!

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:30.830
But...

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:34.670
"The enemy is equipped with Gravity Blast Cannons."

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.620
Is that what's on your mind?

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.580
Don't worry.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.440
That's why we have the Phase Transition Engine.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:41.490
That's why we have the Distortion Field.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:44.420
And the Gravity Blast Cannon.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.990
It's different from the battle you fought.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.650
Please, you may rest easy.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:57.000
Enemy battleship strengthening field.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:57.910
What!

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:02.350
Damn them, a field?.

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.890
Guess, Shinigami is insight.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:05.300
Yeah, right!

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:11.510
Damn!

00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.300
Come on!

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.960
Damn! The enemy are using fields too.

00:04:21.960 --> 00:04:23.250
It's dangerous, butt head!

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:24.040
I'm sorry!

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:26.960
It started cool, but that kamikaze attack ended up looking silly.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:29.050
I'll make sure to gather your remains.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:30.670
Izumi!

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:32.950
What should we do? If it's like this...

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:34.120
I know!

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.560
Hey, Tenkawa! That's nuts!

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.060
You're not serious about a kamikaze?!

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.120
Of course not!

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.250
Change the angle...

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.560
Gekigan Shoot!

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.800
Eighty percent of all enemy units to our bow have been vaporized.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.260
Re-entry navigation possible.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:21.080
Here.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.370
Thank you, Ruri-ruri.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.760
Okay, everyone ready?

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.330
This will get bumpy for awhile.

00:05:28.330 --> 00:05:30.150
Before that, recall the Aestivalis.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:31.090
I'm way ahead of you.

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:42.580
It's on me.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.150
I was so surprised.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:46.480
Just like this.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.570
We're just saying you're pretty good.

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:51.400
Take it.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:57.700
Proceeding through Mars thermosphere.

00:05:57.700 --> 00:06:00.040
Phase Transition Engine reaction power is decreasing.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:00.740
What's that?

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:02.910
Those are nanomachine collectives.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.100
Nano?

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.440
Nanomachines.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.260
Very small self-replicating machinery.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:12.960
They used them in order to create an atmosphere similar to Earth.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:17.340
Yes, they're continuing their work to create a stable atmosphere.

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:18.960
But they also function as shields,

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:22.020
protecting the surface from harmful radiation from space,

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.530
even though there are no longer any people left to benefit.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.390
Passing through the first layer of nanomachines.

00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:32.200
Isn't it harmful to have something like that enter the Nadesico?

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.560
There's nothing to worry about.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.940
Everyone on Mars was breathing air made partially of them.

00:06:37.940 --> 00:06:40.950
They're harmless. They come out the other end in the bathroom.

00:06:40.950 --> 00:06:41.870
Oh, dear me!

00:06:41.870 --> 00:06:44.420
That's right. Captain, you were born on Mars, weren't you?

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:47.160
Is that so?

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:49.570
Gravity Blast Cannon, standby.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.660
Sure, but why not use it before, from space?

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:56.290
A second wave should be awaiting us on the surface.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:58.090
We will decimate them before they surround us.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.490
Please aim the bow toward the enemy.

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.850
Let's have some gravitational buffering down here!

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:08.690
Damn! Why does he get all the chicks?

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:26.200
All enemy units vaporized.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:29.420
No signs of Jovian activity within a 30km radius of the Nadesico.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:35.120
We will now prepare a landing party

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:37.260
and send them to the surface in the landing ship, Hinagiku.

00:07:37.470 --> 00:07:39.380
But where shall we go?

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:43.930
From satellite orbital observation,
there appear to be no active colonies remaining.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:47.660
First we will head toward Nergal's research facility at Olympus Mons.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:48.830
Nergal's?

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:50.300
Shrewd businessmen, aren't we?

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.230
Our research facility is like a shelter actually.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:55.860
It seems to be the most likely spot for survivors.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:58.280
Now, the landing party...

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:01.310
Excuse me, I'd like to borrow an Aestivalis.

00:08:01.310 --> 00:08:02.160
What?

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.280
I'd like to have a look at the Utopia Colony.

00:08:05.150 --> 00:08:06.360
The place you were born?

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:11.250
There's nothing left there anymore.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.470
And there's a Chulip near there.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:15.060
I know, but...

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:17.330
I'd just like to have another look.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:18.560
But...

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.300
Go ahead!

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.050
But, Sir!

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.420
I'm well aware that I am merely an ornament here,

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:27.590
but I seem to recall I'm in charge of combat operations, Goat-kun.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.530
Everyone should have the right to see their homeland,

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.160
especially if they're still young.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:33.680
Thank you very much, Sir!

00:08:36.010 --> 00:08:37.360
Hinagiku, taking off!

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:48.770
Tekawa unit, route A B C No.7...   Tenkawa unit, route A B C No.7...

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:50.250
What are you doing! You'll get hurt!

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:51.010
Tekawa unit, route A B C No.7...   Tenkawa unit, route A B C No.7...

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.420
Megumi-san

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:52.630
Tekawa unit, route A B C No.7...   Tenkawa unit, route A B C No.7...

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.720
Would you mind if I tag along?

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:57.170
Why?

00:08:57.650 --> 00:08:59.840
I'd like to see your hometown.

00:09:00.110 --> 00:09:01.630
That's for only one person!

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.500
Why is it always him?!

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.040
I have no idea.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.070
They say those who look the most unlikely actually get the...

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:09.060
Don't give me that!

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.900
Wow! This is spectacular!

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:18.080
Is the place you lived far?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:23.850
We have problem here!

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:25.570
Right?!

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:26.960
It's no big deal.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:28.460
There are no enemies approaching.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:29.910
Even without a communications officer.

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:32.230
Well, that might be the case, but...

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:39.750
Where will you be, Captain?

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:40.930
Well...

00:09:41.670 --> 00:09:45.260
I know! Jun-kun, would you be in charge for awhile?

00:09:45.570 --> 00:09:47.140
I can't do that without good reason.

00:09:47.140 --> 00:09:47.960
Bummer...

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:49.830
Captain
Then how's this?

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:50.260
Captain

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:52.800
Well, I guess I'll be...

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:53.690
No way!

00:09:58.520 --> 00:10:00.150
You'd probably do a better job.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:10.350
No good. It looks like it's been abandoned for months.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:13.530
Looks like they ran off long ago.

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:17.230
What kind of research were you doing in the middle of nowhere?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:18.320
It was for the Nadesico.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:20.970
Really?

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:22.040
Would you be interested

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:24.800
in seeing the beginnings of the Nadesico?

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.340
Please take a look.

00:10:40.060 --> 00:10:42.950
It's been about ten years since colonization began,

00:10:42.950 --> 00:10:47.200
so I think that would make it thirty years ago,

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:48.450
when this was first discovered.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:58.540
Can I ask you something?

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:00.090
Sure.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:03.010
Were you close to the Captain's family?

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.720
They were servicemen stationed here.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.790
My parents were scientists.

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:10.550
I guess that doesn't matter to children, does it?

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:11.260
I suppose...

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.170
Look at me, Akito! Launch arm!

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:18.320
Hey, Yurika! You're not supposed to be in there on your own!

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.050
It's all right. Start engines, forward launch!

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.150
What is it?

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:27.070
Darn it!

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:42.850
In the end, I was the one blamed for messing with the machine.

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:47.740
What really frustrated me was that I couldn't control the machine.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:50.110
I guess that's why I got this.

00:11:52.280 --> 00:11:53.220
What about being a cook?

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:56.210
What made you decide to become a cook?

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:00.400
Well, it's because the food here is just terrible.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:02.300
Take a look.

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:03.570
See?

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:10.630
But what are these?

00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:12.060
Nanomachines.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.350
The same things that we saw in the sky?

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:14.660
Yeah.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:18.440
Thanks to these little guys, the air has gotten much better,

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:20.260
but the soil still has a long way to go.

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.380
Vegetables don't taste too good here.

00:12:22.820 --> 00:12:25.590
But when a cook gets through with them, they taste delicious.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:28.340
It's like magic to me. That's why...

00:12:28.690 --> 00:12:31.670
That's why you wanted to become a cook! Right?

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.300
Yeah...

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:34.800
So cute!

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:35.790
Cu...!

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:38.130
But now you're a pilot.

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:42.080
Yeah, guess I'm kind of wishy-washy.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.280
Oh no, you're not!

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:45.170
You're nothing of the sort!

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:46.230
Definitely not.

00:12:46.900 --> 00:12:49.360
You're always trying your best, Akito.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:50.360
You're doing your best.

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:52.880
Is there something wrong?

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.130
Nothing...

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:57.120
Did I say something that offended you?

00:12:57.450 --> 00:12:59.790
No, it's just...

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.890
Am I saying something strange?

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:06.090
No, but you see...

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:10.630
About before, I was just really happy, so...

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:14.690
When I quit my last job, I looked forward to this,

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:17.130
not irresponsible or half-hearted,

00:13:17.450 --> 00:13:19.560
but someone sincere and determined.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:23.400
Akito-san, that's why I...

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.990
Akito-san? Akito-san?

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.800
Ouch...

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:35.520
Akito-san? Akito-san!

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.890
Welcome to Mars.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:43.170
I think it would be a good idea to get off of him.

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:47.000
I'm not sure whether to welcome you or throw you out.

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:50.060
In either case, let me at least treat you to some coffee.

00:14:03.710 --> 00:14:05.430
I suppose I need to do some explaining.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:09.300
Survivors from the other colonies have gathered here as well.

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:12.340
The Jovian Lizards aren't interested in people.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:13.150
Thank goodness!

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:15.180
You guys made it!

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:16.120
You can go home now!

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:17.240
You can all go back to Earth!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:19.390
We came to help you guys out!

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:20.880
Our ship can...

00:14:20.880 --> 00:14:21.790
They won't be boarding.

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.380
Why not?

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:24.830
I'll explain that now.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:27.130
I didn't ask for an in-depth explanation.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:30.160
Do you honestly think that one battleship can escape from Mars?

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:31.790
There are many more enemy units nearby.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:35.660
We fought our way here, and we've made it this far!

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.200
You don't know the strength of the Nadesico...

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:39.670
With the Phase Transition Engine?

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:41.200
Hey, who are you?

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:46.840
I'm one of the researchers who developed the
Phase Transition Engine and the Distortion Field.

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:48.190
Inez Fressange.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:50.320
In other words...

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:51.150
You work with Nergal?

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:59.220
Hello, Akito! Akito!

00:14:59.940 --> 00:15:02.400
I was worried, so I came anyway!

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:04.870
Worried about what, I won't ask.

00:15:05.350 --> 00:15:06.580
Tenkawa and the others confirmed.

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.130
In other words, "Go away now."

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:15.800
Is that what you're saying?

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:18.130
We will remain on Mars.

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:20.450
I'm the one who did the principal designing of the Nadesico

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:22.580
and sent those designs back to Earth.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:23.970
That's how I know.

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.310
This ship cannot stand against the Jovian Lizards.

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.770
I have no intention of boarding such a ship.

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:30.650
Sorry to contradict you, Lady,

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:34.690
but we've won all our engagements with the Jovians.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:36.740
That's why...

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:37.840
All right, then!

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:41.940
How much do you know about the Jovian Lizards?

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:44.680
How do you think such advanced unmanned weapons were made?

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:46.420
What about their goals?

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.000
Why have they occupied Mars?

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:49.910
Can't you believe in us?

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.570
What if I analyze what's going through your mind right now.

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:55.480
You've managed to score some points in battle.

00:15:55.480 --> 00:15:57.400
You went on a date with your girl.

00:15:57.760 --> 00:15:59.410
So, "I can do anything!"

00:16:00.050 --> 00:16:02.080
Are you hooked on explaining and analyzing?

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.870
It's a real mistake to think that your youth makes you invincible.

00:16:06.370 --> 00:16:08.180
Not everyone can become a hero.

00:16:08.180 --> 00:16:09.020
Fressange-san!

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:11.280
Incoming enemy.

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:13.710
Five large battleships.

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:15.020
Thirty smaller warships.

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:16.940
Gravity Blast at full power!

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:18.450
Full power, okay!

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:20.360
Gravity Blast energy charging.

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:23.450
Fire!

00:16:27.520 --> 00:16:28.690
We did it!

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.170
They withstood a Gravity Blast?

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:37.910
The enemy is also using a Distortion Field.

00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:40.950
Neither side will be able to wipe out the other in one sweep.

00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:48.520
Enemy is reinforcing its numbers from the Chulip 40km ahead.

00:16:48.950 --> 00:16:51.350
What's going on? How can there be so many in that thing?

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:54.270
They're not coming out of it. They're coming through it.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:17:01.780
In a never-ending flow, those warships are being sent through from another place!

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.050
Enemy continues to reinforce.

00:17:05.350 --> 00:17:07.070
Their field is not invincible.

00:17:07.390 --> 00:17:08.240
We must fire continuously!

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:11.250
Yes! Gravity Blast Cannon, standby!

00:17:11.250 --> 00:17:12.150
I can't.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.580
We're not in a vacuum.

00:17:14.870 --> 00:17:19.030
The reaction power of the Phase Transition Engine is not enough for continuous Gravity Blast discharges.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:22.730
What do we do?

00:17:22.730 --> 00:17:25.340
They'll turn us into mincemeat in no time with those numbers.

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:26.970
Raise the Distortion Field!

00:17:27.030 --> 00:17:27.410
Wait!...

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:28.240
Wait!

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:30.010
Wait! If we raise the Distortion Field now,

00:17:30.010 --> 00:17:32.390
the ground underneath the Nadesico will cave in.

00:17:32.570 --> 00:17:36.310
All of Inez-san's friends, all the survivors are concentrated there!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:42.280
Take off immediately and raise the field as altitude...

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:46.850
I'm sorry, but once we've landed, it takes a while before we can take off again.

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:50.020
Enemy fleet positioning over the Nadesico.

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:52.440
The Chulip continues to reinforce the enemy's numbers.

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:56.170
Raise the field, or take on the enemy's attack without it?

00:17:56.170 --> 00:17:59.060
Admiral, it looks like this decision is too much for the Captain.

00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:00.380
We'll have to...

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:01.420
But Akito has...

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:03.940
He made a promise to those people underground!

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:07.740
That we'd come back for them and take them back to Earth!

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:09.480
How can you?!

00:18:11.550 --> 00:18:12.180
Akito...

00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:15.950
Enemy vessels have stopped moving.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:17.020
Attack imminent.

00:18:17.390 --> 00:18:19.940
This is no time to be indecisive. Activate automatic defenses now!

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:21.830
But the Captain has still not given the order.

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:26.280
Sensors indicate graviton wave concentration.

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:51.060
It may have been that our fates were sealed when the Chulips rained on Mars.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:53.640
Even without activating field, with this rain of fire...

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:59.410
In any case, it looks like you were unable to become heroes.

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:02.810
Yurika!

00:19:02.810 --> 00:19:04.400
Retreat while continuing to maintain the field.

00:19:04.400 --> 00:19:06.700
Return enemy fire once enough distance has been obtained.

00:19:07.010 --> 00:19:08.570
Continue to monitor field...

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:23.190
What was the point of us coming to Mars?

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:26.430
Akito, I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:29.910
I couldn't save them at all!

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:31.720
Yurika...

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:37.620
This is the first time

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:40.620
that you've been nice to me since we came aboard the Nadesico.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:43.290
Stop it! Pull yourself together!

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:44.710
Akito...

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:47.900
Would you give me a kiss?

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:50.200
Yurika? What are you saying?

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:53.980
It isn't that! What you did with Megumi-san isn't what's on my mind.

00:19:54.280 --> 00:19:55.590
You were watching?

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:58.330
Well, you see, that was...

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:02.860
If you could give me a kiss, that would keep me going.

00:20:04.190 --> 00:20:05.960
It would keep me going just a little longer.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:11.770
I'm sorry!

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:13.350
Akito...

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:15.720
Megumi-san...

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.170
Yurika-san,

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:19.500
I don't care if I am his refuge.

00:20:20.270 --> 00:20:21.270
I'm not going to lose.

00:20:23.710 --> 00:20:25.020
I'm not going to lose either!

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:28.860
We'll beat back the Jovian Lizards together!

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:29.880
Yeah...

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:31.860
They're not going to keep me down! No way!

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:36.420
Captain, that's not what I meant.

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:39.250
Come on, let me explain what I meant!

00:21:45.160 --> 00:21:48.550
The invincible Nadesico can withstand any attack.

00:21:48.550 --> 00:21:51.040
But as the diabolical might of the mysterious battleships

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:53.340
encroaches ever closer, the Nadesico is forced to embark...

00:21:53.340 --> 00:21:56.320
Upon her final voyage?!

00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:58.780
This is the greatest popular show filled with limitless,

00:21:58.780 --> 00:22:01.000
soul-stirring intensity and beautiful romantic narrative!

00:22:01.130 --> 00:22:04.030
Hark! The Nadesico is going down!

00:22:04.030 --> 00:22:06.180
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:06.180 --> 00:22:08.500
"The Song That You Will Sing One Day"

00:22:08.740 --> 00:22:10.660
Let's watch it, everyone!
